        "html": "<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The whole café. 2. Owen had asked about front-counter help before. 3. That Grace organizes labels better than he does. 4. Whether a real responsibility is being offered. 5. No. 6. Old photographs from the former bookshop.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Grammar Refresh</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>kidding  2. serious  3. meant  4. like  5. up</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>A. 理解检查</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>F  2. T  3. F  4. F  5. T  6. F</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>B. 意图、效果、修复</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>intention  2. effect  3. repair</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>C. 参考</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Are you serious?</strong></li>\n<li><strong>I thought you meant the meeting was canceled.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>I didn&#39;t realize it sounded like a real request.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Thanks for clearing that up.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<h3>E. Lesson 29间隔检索参考</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Can we talk about the changed plan?</strong></li>\n<li><strong>I feel excluded when decisions are announced before we discuss them.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>What happened was the message went out before our call.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>I need us to check the calendar first.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>I&#39;m not asking you to cancel every plan.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>What would help is one message before the announcement.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>开放题必须区分原意和效果。玩笑是否合适不能只由说话者单方面决定。</p>\n<hr>\n"
