      {
        "id": "section-5",
        "title": "5. What People Actually Say",
        "html": "<h3>本课负荷说明</h3>\n<p>本课有6项全新主动表达。第40课的建议词块在主对话与练习中近距离复现。</p>\n<h3>1. The one next to …</h3>\n<p>……旁边的那个。中性；当双方都知道在比较哪类物品时使用。</p>\n<h3>2. The rail that …</h3>\n<p>那个……的轨道。<code>that</code>后提供识别该物品所必需的信息。</p>\n<h3>3. The person who …</h3>\n<p>那个……的人。<code>who</code>指人，帮助确认职责或身份。</p>\n<h3>4. The place where …</h3>\n<p>……的地方。<code>where</code>指地点，可替代较长的 <code>the place in which …</code>。</p>\n<h3>5. Do you mean the one that …?</h3>\n<p>你指的是那个……的吗？中性；相似对象较多时主动核对。</p>\n<h3>6. That&#39;s the one.</h3>\n<p>就是那个。中性、自然；只在前文特征已经足够明确时使用。</p>\n<h3>Don&#39;t Say It That Way</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>容易说出的句子</th>\n<th>更准确的表达</th>\n<th>原因</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>The rail which next to elevator.</td>\n<td>The rail <strong>that is next to the elevator</strong>.</td>\n<td>从句需要主语和动词</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>The person which handles repairs.</td>\n<td>The person <strong>who handles repairs</strong>.</td>\n<td>指人优先用<code>who</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>The place which we met there.</td>\n<td>The place <strong>where we met</strong>.</td>\n<td><code>where</code>后不再加<code>there</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fix that one.</td>\n<td>Please check <strong>rail L-2, the short one above the narrow bench</strong>.</td>\n<td>单独<code>that one</code>可能指错</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "section-6",
        "title": "6. Grammar Refresh — 限定性关系从句",
        "html": "<h3>1. who：识别人</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The staff member <strong>who manages contractor visits</strong> is Sam.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>2. that：识别物</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The rail <strong>that faces the service desk</strong> is L-2.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>口语中指物也常用 <code>which</code>；本课主动练习先用高频 <code>that</code>。</p>\n<h3>3. where：识别地点</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is the place <strong>where we noticed the movement</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>4. 为什么这些信息不能删？</h3>\n<p>这里有不止一个工作人员、不止一条轨道。关系从句回答“到底是哪一个”，因此不加逗号。本课不教授补充性非限定关系从句。</p>\n<h3>快速练习</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The technician __________ visited yesterday left a card.</li>\n<li>The rail __________ ends beside the gallery needs attention.</li>\n<li>This is the place __________ the bracket moved.</li>\n<li>Do you mean the door __________ faces the elevator?</li>\n<li>Sam is the person __________ arranges contractor visits.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "section-7",
        "title": "7. Sound Natural — 用重音把相似对象分开",
        "html": "<blockquote>\n<p>The <strong>SHORT</strong> rail / that ends beside the <strong>GALLERY</strong>.<br>Not the <strong>LONG</strong> one / above the brochure <strong>TABLE</strong>.<br>The staff member / who handles <strong>FACILITIES</strong> requests.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>关系词通常不重读；真正区分对象的名词、形容词和地点需要清楚。对比时把 <code>short / long</code> 读出差别。</p>\n<h3>影子跟读</h3>\n<p>先读完整特征，再缩短为 <code>That&#39;s the one</code>。如果听者还不能指出对象，就不能过早缩短。</p>\n<hr>\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "section-8",
        "title": "8. Practice",
        "html": "<h3>A. 理解检查</h3>\n<p>判断 True 或 False。</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Rail L-1 is being reported.</li>\n<li>Rail L-2 is above a narrow bench.</li>\n<li>Daniel knows why the bracket moved.</li>\n<li>Test materials had already been removed.</li>\n<li>Sam manages contractor visits.</li>\n<li>Lena decides to repair the bracket herself.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>B. 选择 who / that / where</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The worker __________ called this morning is Sam.</li>\n<li>The bracket __________ moved is on the left.</li>\n<li>The lobby is the place __________ visitors enter.</li>\n<li>The note __________ includes code L-2 is accurate.</li>\n<li>The person __________ receives the report works in facilities.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>C. 合并句子</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The short rail needs attention. It ends beside the gallery.</li>\n<li>Sam is the coordinator. He manages contractor visits.</li>\n<li>This is the lobby wall. We noticed the movement here.</li>\n<li>The long rail is secure. It hangs above the brochure table.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>D. Lesson 40近距离检索</h3>\n<p>不看第40课，用完整英文回应。</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Ask Daniel what he would do while the location is waiting for inspection.</li>\n<li>Give advice from Daniel&#39;s point of view without taking over Lena&#39;s decision.</li>\n<li>State the main trade-off between closing the lobby and keeping one rail unused.</li>\n<li>Name the lowest-risk temporary response.</li>\n<li>Say the response can be reviewed if facilities gives new instructions.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>E. 平面图信息差</h3>\n<p>伙伴A只能看第3部分平面图，伙伴B只能看以下工单：</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>“Please inspect the display rail near the elevator. One bracket moves.”</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>B必须追问，A必须用 <code>who / that / where</code> 补齐。最后共同形成包含 <code>floor / code / landmark / part / observation</code> 的维修位置描述。</p>\n<h3>F. 实用写作：维修位置报告</h3>\n<p>写80—120词给Sam。必须包括：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>平面图代码L-2；</li>\n<li>两个地标；</li>\n<li>与L-1的区别；</li>\n<li>松动的是哪个部件；</li>\n<li>只报告观察，不推断原因；</li>\n<li>当前临时措施。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>G. 中译英情境表达</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>是电梯旁边的那个。</li>\n<li>是那个朝向服务台的短轨道。</li>\n<li>Sam是安排承包商来访的人。</li>\n<li>这是我们注意到支架移动的地方。</li>\n<li>你指的是那个延伸到前门的长轨道吗？</li>\n<li>对，就是那个。</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "section-9",
        "title": "9. Make It Yours",
        "html": "<h3>现实定位任务</h3>\n<p>选择家中、办公室或公共场所一个无安全风险、适合报告的问题，例如坏椅子、标签错误或不工作的灯。画一个简单平面图，标出两个相似对象。</p>\n<h3>2分钟说明</h3>\n<p>只看图，不写完整稿。至少使用一个 <code>who</code>、两个 <code>that</code> 和一个 <code>where</code> 从句。请听者复述具体对象；如果复述错误，补充地标而不是重复 <code>that one</code>。</p>\n<h3>三天后的间隔复习</h3>\n<p>换一张新平面图，在60秒内确认地点、物品和负责人。准确优先于速度。</p>\n<hr>\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "section-10",
        "title": "10. Answer Key",
        "html": "<h3>Check the story</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>The short rail L-2 next to the elevator, above the narrow bench. 2. The long rail L-1 above the brochure table. 3. The left bracket moved slightly when the empty rail was touched. 4. Nothing; test materials had been removed. 5. The facilities coordinator who manages contractor visits. 6. Mark only L-2 unavailable and ask Sam to confirm the next step.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>第3部分</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>L-1. 2. L-2. 3. Beside the end of L-2. 4. The left bracket on L-2.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Grammar Refresh</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>who  2. that  3. where  4. that  5. who</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>A. 理解检查</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>F  2. T  3. F  4. T  5. T  6. F</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>B. 选择</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>who  2. that  3. where  4. that  5. who</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>C. 合并句子参考</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>The short rail that ends beside the gallery needs attention.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sam is the coordinator who manages contractor visits.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This is the lobby wall where we noticed the movement.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The long rail that hangs above the brochure table is secure.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<h3>D. Lesson 40近距离检索参考</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>What would you do while we wait for the inspection?</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If I were you, I&#39;d keep the rail unused.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The main trade-off is access versus disruption.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The safest option is to keep only L-2 unavailable.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>We can revisit it if facilities gives new instructions.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<h3>F. 实用写作参考</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hi Sam, please inspect display rail L-2 in the first-floor lobby. It is the short rail that is next to the elevator and above the narrow bench. It faces the service desk and ends beside the side-gallery entrance. It is not L-1, the long rail above the brochure table. The left bracket on L-2 moved slightly when the empty rail was touched. We did not identify the cause, and no materials were attached. We have marked L-2 as unavailable until facilities confirms the next step. Please let us know whether you need another photo or measurement.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>G. 中译英参考</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>It&#39;s the one next to the elevator.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>It&#39;s the short rail that faces the service desk.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sam is the person who arranges contractor visits.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>This is the place where we noticed the bracket move.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Do you mean the long rail that runs toward the front doors?</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Yes, that&#39;s the one.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>开放题答案不唯一，但必须提供足以区分相似对象的特征，不能推断故障原因。</p>\n<hr>\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "section-11",
        "title": "11. Self-check",
        "html": "<p>为每项选择：<strong>能做到／还不稳定／需要重学</strong>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>我能用 <code>who</code> 识别相关人员。</li>\n<li>我能用 <code>that</code> 区分相似物品。</li>\n<li>我能用 <code>where</code> 识别地点。</li>\n<li>我能根据平面图提供代码、地标和具体部件。</li>\n<li>我能把观察和原因推断分开。</li>\n<li>我能写一则80—120词的准确维修位置报告。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>若有两项以上选择“需要重学”，先重做第5部分和第7部分B—F；三天后换一张平面图再完成一次定位。</p>\n"
      }
